{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011Cd558Q5vEpXMpumfhjSfk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN\n// Strategy: GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan for GSM symbolic tasks.\n// We inject task guidance directing the LM to reason freely in plain text then\n// emit exactly ONE constrained answer span <<expr>> at the end.\n// A 75%-of-budget free-text prefix budget lets the model complete multi-step\n// arithmetic reasoning before the parser takes over inside the span.\n// When maxSteps == 0 we short-circuit immediately; the progress postcondition\n// is satisfied by the `maxSteps == 0` disjunct.\n// cost is set to maxSteps (>0 when we generate) satisfying `cost > 0` for the\n// progress disjunct, and `cost <= maxSteps` by direct assignment.\n// CSD_RATIONALE_END\n\n// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN\n// Invariant 1 (parser_validity):\n//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)\n//   - Before the branch: currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained, and the\n//     method precondition asserts insideConstrained ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrained),\n//     so the invariant holds trivially for the zero-budget path.\n//   - In the else branch: GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan discharges this proof\n//     obligation internally; its postcondition guarantees that on return\n//     insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).\n//\n// Invariant 2 (progress): |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps\n//   - Zero-budget path: generated == generatedPrefix and steps == cost == 0,\n//     so |generated| == |generatedPrefix| + 0.\n//   - Else branch: GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan is bounded by maxSteps\n//     total token-steps, so it appends at most maxSteps visible tokens to the\n//     input generatedPrefix. We set cost := maxSteps, giving\n//     |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps == |generatedPrefix| + cost.\n//     Tokens consumed by EOS or delimiter helpers count toward cost but do not\n//     exceed the budget, so the bound is always satisfied.\n// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END\n\ngenerated := generatedPrefix;\ninsideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;\ncurrentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;\ncost := 0;\n\nif maxSteps == 0 {\n  // Zero budget: all postconditions satisfied by maxSteps == 0 disjunct.\n} else {\n  helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, \"Solve step by step in plain text. At the very END, write the final answer as exactly ONE <<expr>>. Combine ALL parts of the calculation into this ONE expression. Example: <<int(n * frac_1 * frac_2)>> or <<total // n1 + (total * t) // n2>>. Inside <<>>: variable names without braces (n not {n}, frac_1 not {frac_1}), integers, +, -, *, /, //, %, (, ), int() ONLY. Use // for integer division. FORBIDDEN inside <<>>: max(), min(), abs(), floor(), ceil(), {braces}, $, **, LaTeX, HTML tags, any other functions. Do NOT write multiple <<>> blocks for intermediate steps — ONE final <<expr>> only.\");\n\n  var prefixBudget: nat := (maxSteps * 75) / 100;\n  if prefixBudget >= maxSteps {\n    prefixBudget := maxSteps - 1;\n  }\n\n  var g, ic, cc := helpers.GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan(\n    lm, parser, prompt, generated, insideConstrainedOut, currentConstrainedOut,\n    maxSteps, prefixBudget, validTokenGroups, 10.0, 8, eosToken\n  );\n  generated := g;\n  insideConstrainedOut := ic;\n  currentConstrainedOut := cc;\n\n  cost := maxSteps;\n}"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10414,"cache_read_input_tokens":1145,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10414},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60cee6dd-2dc5-44de-af73-612192a6e97e","uuid":"25c0ff6f-bcde-4936-9bb6-5f41c7b9e46c","request_id":"req_011Cd558NjKBQSA6JhDpVYc